            <!-- ===================================================== -->
            <!-- SUMMARY -->
            <!-- ===================================================== -->

            <h3 class="h3 fw-bold text-dark mt-4 mb-3">
                Summary
            </h3>

            <div class="alert alert-primary border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">

                <ul class="mb-0">

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Encapsulation is an important principle of OOP.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        It combines related data and behavior inside a class.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        It helps control how data can be accessed or modified.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Private members help hide internal data from direct
                        outside access.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Public methods and properties can provide controlled access.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Validation can be performed before changing important data.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Properties such as <b>get; private set;</b> are commonly
                        used to control access.
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        Encapsulation makes applications easier to maintain,
                        understand, and protect.
                    </li>

                </ul>

            </div>


